  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cef97c8bb4a2e1f4c8da884146093661, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::EndingScreenController
  endingPanel: {fileID: 571459661}
  endingText: {fileID: 1230233782}
  endingContent: 'You: I have learnt so many things from these short 5 days! I''ve
    learnt that


    - Jaywalking is dangerous even if it''s convenient, and many
    people still do it. We need to put an end to it, especially with how normalised
    it is, with young adults to literal children doing it.


    - We must always
    practise special awareness when on the road, and ensure our transportation vehicle
    is not faulty before using it. Wearing protective gear is also very much recommended,
    as it can literally save your life in critical cases.


    - We must stay focused
    on the road, especially when traversing dangerous parts. Having awareness and
    knowing what is going on around you is a huge help, and can even save you from
    life or death cases, especially as a pedestrian.


    You: Thank you for going
    on this journey, and I hope you learnt something important from this. Most importantly,
    I hope you had fun playing.'
  playerInteraction: {fileID: 1640700288}
